  "text": "As soon as it was early morning, the chief priest, Selders, and teachers, law on the whole high court, had Jesus tied up and then handed him over to the Roman Governor pilot. \"So pilot, too, examined him, are you King of the Jews?\" he said. \"And an answer,\" he says. \"Your words not mine.\" Now the chief priest had charged him with many things, so pilot again interrogated him. \"You're not answering anything like it as long as to charges, but Jesus didn't answer any firm.\" there which astonished Pilot. That was accustomed to festival for him to release a prisoner as requested by the people. There was a man named Barabbas who was imprisoned with some terrorists who had killed people during an uprising. The crowd came up and asked Pilot to do for them what he usually did, and Pilot answered them, saying, \"Do you always release to you this King of the Jews?\" for he knew that the chief priest's main reason for handing him over was envy of Jesus' popularity.",
